## How to build, run, test

### Build (incremental, ~20 min on warm caches)

```bash
./scripts/chromium/build.sh
```

Full rebuilds only when you `rm -rf chromium/src/out/Default` or bump Chromium pin. Expect ~3-4h.

### Run (GUI window)

```bash
./scripts/chromium/run.sh -- --slayzone-layout-shell --user-data-dir=$(mktemp -d -t slayzone)
```

Add `--enable-logging=stderr --v=0` to see `[sidecar]`, `[layout]`, and C++ INFO lines in your terminal.

### Run (headless + CDP for scripted tests)

```bash
APP=chromium/src/out/Default/SlayZone.app/Contents/MacOS/SlayZone
"$APP" --headless=new --disable-gpu --no-first-run --no-default-browser-check \
  --allow-chrome-scheme-url --slayzone-layout-shell \
  --user-data-dir=$(mktemp -d) --remote-debugging-port=9666 \
  --enable-logging=stderr --v=0 "chrome://slayzone-shell/" \
  > /tmp/slayzone.log 2>&1 &
```

Drive via CDP at `http://localhost:9666/json` or `ws://localhost:9666/devtools/page/<id>`.

### Verify

```bash
node tools/verify/part-i-final.js           # 22 Part I tests (expect 22/22)
bash scripts/chromium/phase-6-verify.sh      # Phase 6 scripted sweep
```

### Patch workflow (when editing chromium/src)

```bash
# edit chromium/src/... directly
./scripts/chromium/build.sh                  # verify builds
# if the change should stick:
cd chromium/src && git add -A && git commit -m "slayzone: <description>"
cd ../..
git -C chromium/src format-patch -1 HEAD \
  --output-directory patches/chromium/ \
  --start-number <NEXT> \
  --subject-prefix="slayzone"
git add patches/chromium/<NNNN>-*.patch
git commit -m "feat(chromium): <description>"
```

### Outer-repo commits

```bash
git add <paths>
git commit -m "feat(chromium): <description>"   # or feat(shared), feat(sidecar), fix(<scope>), chore(<scope>)
```

Never skip signing (`--no-gpg-sign`) unless 1Password SSH agent has genuinely lapsed — ask the user to unlock first.

